ely cannot beat it (only two Aces left unaccounted for, and they’re split between two players — unlikely either has a pair). This will probably win, letting me keep playing on next round.\n- Play **rocket**: overkill now. No benefit — wastes the only unbeatable move when not under threat.\n\nSince I want to maintain initiative, starting with a **high pair like ♠A ♥A** is ideal. It’s very strong — only a bomb or rocket can beat it, and neither peasant has shown aggression. With only 2 Aces unaccounted (and none known), it\'s highly unlikely either holds AA. So this will almost certainly win, letting me continue playing.\n\nAlternatively, I could play a single high card (like RedJoker), but that would waste its power unnecessarily — jokers are best saved for escaping tight spots.\n\nThus, **♠A ♥A** is the optimal move: high enough to win, uses a clean pair, and advances my hand efficiently.\n\nReason:  \nPlaying ♠A ♥A as a pair maximizes the chance of winning the trick and retaining the lead, while being highly unlikely to be beaten by either peasant (who each have 17 cards but probably don’t hold a pair of Aces). This allows me to continue playing on my next turn, progressing toward emptying my hand. Saving the rocket and high singles like jokers for later traps is prudent.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠A", "♥A"]}'}
