omething**, and I should avoid wasting powerful singles.\n\nThe optimal strategy is to **play small-to-medium pairs first**, preserving rockets and bombs.\n\nEither pair works. Let\'s pick the **pair of 8s** as it’s lower and safer.\n\nBut wait — Valid Moves list shows:\n- pair: ♥8 ♣8\n- pair: ♠10 ♦10\n\nSo both are explicitly allowed.\n\nFinal decision: Play **♥8 ♣8** — a safe, efficient way to reduce hand size without overcommitting.\n\nReason: It removes two cards, maintains control by setting a low bar that likely won’t trigger a bomb, and preserves higher pairs and the rocket for future protection.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥8", "♣8"]}'}
